    "sensesNotes": "Keen Smell",
    "tactics": "Hunting Dogs work ahead of their handlers, locate prey, and drive it toward waiting hunters. They avoid trading bites with heavily armored creatures and use speed to keep wounded prey from escaping.",
    "attacksNotes": "<p>Bite [Combat]: Melee attack (Agil 6 + Melee Combat 1), Reach: 5 ft</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Margin 1:</strong>: 8 damage (5 + 3 Str)</li>\n<li><strong>Margin 2:</strong> 8 damage, DR halved (round up)</li>\n</ul>",
    "specialAbilitiesNotes": "<p>Keen Smell: Scent-based Perception checks have Fortune. Track by Scent: The Hunting Dog has Fortune on Wilderness checks to follow a creature that has passed through the area within the last day. Flush Prey: Once per encounter, when the Hunting Dog hits a Hidden or Concealed target, that target loses Hidden and cannot benefit from Concealed against the dog's allies until the start of the dog's next turn.</p>",
